/-!
# Counted Simon decoding

`simonDecodedRun` applies the register decoder to fresh character samples and attaches query,
gate, and sample counts. `simonPreparedCircuit` includes the Hadamard preparation needed to
start from a zero basis state.

The success bounds use either the intrinsic orthogonal rank or the accessible budget `n + k`,
following the sampling principle of [Simon1997].

## Main statements

* `simon_decoder_actual_output_mass`: expresses decoded output mass as a sum over records.
* `simon_gaussian_accessible_budget`: bounds success and failure after `n + k` samples.
* `simon_actual_preparation_and_quantum_cost`: verifies preparation and exact circuit counts.

## References

* [Simon, 1997][Simon1997]
-/

open Qatlib.Concepts.WalkFind.UniformThree
open Qatlib.Concepts.LinearLearning.ConcisePipeline.CostedLaw
open Qatlib.Concepts.HspRecovery.Distinguisher
